<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Scott returns three months after his blood pressure was first found to be raised and about eight weeks before he leaves. His home readings over the last week average 134/85 mmHg, despite less salt, regular training and keeping alcohol within limits. He has finished a four-day wilderness first aid course, including frostbite, hypothermia, rewarming, splinting, and packaging a casualty in a sledge. He has not smoked for thirteen weeks and wants to keep taking varenicline through the voyage, when he fears the craving will return. He feels well and is sleeping well. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Seven-day average 134/85 mmHg after three months of lifestyle measures</td></tr><tr><td>Training</td><td>Wilderness first aid course with cold-injury modules completed</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No pipe for thirteen weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Departure</td><td>In about eight weeks</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

