  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension, stage 1, above target after three months of lifestyle measures (I10)</content>. Home average 134/85 mmHg after three months, still above the target below 130/80, so medicine is now advised, as planned at the consultation. Losartan, an angiotensin receptor blocker, is chosen: thiazide diuretics add to fluid and salt loss in the cold and on long marches, and beta-blockers can worsen cold hands and feet and blunt the response to exercise. Starting now leaves about eight weeks to check kidney function and tolerance before departure. [S]<list><item>Start losartan 50 mg daily.</item><item>Sick-day rule, in writing: stop losartan during vomiting, diarrhea, or dehydration, and restart when eating and drinking normally for 24 hours.</item><item>Electrolytes and creatinine in two to four weeks, and before departure.</item><item>Report lightheadedness on standing.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, pipe tobacco, in early remission (F17.290)</content>. Abstinent for thirteen weeks; the first twelve-week course of varenicline is complete. [S]<list><item>Continue varenicline for a second twelve-week course through the voyage, for relapse prevention.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Office blood pressure, validated technique, average of two readings (target below 130/80 mmHg)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>136/86 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Home blood pressure monitoring to confirm the diagnosis and guide treatment</td><td>At diagnosis and when treatment changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seven-day average 134/85 mmHg; above target; losartan started</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI, and cardiac auscultation</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>71.0 kg, BMI 23.7; no murmur</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication adherence, side effects, and sick-day rules</td><td>When starting a medicine, then every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Losartan started; sick-day rule given in writing</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel: sodium, potassium, creatinine, eGFR</td><td>Baseline; 2 to 4 weeks after starting an ARB; then every 6 months on an ARB</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Due two to four weeks after starting losartan</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>8 mg/g at the six-week visit</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fundoscopic examination</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No hypertensive changes at the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>Only for stage 2 hypertension, suspected left ventricular hypertrophy, or clinical change</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Stage 1; no left ventricular hypertrophy</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco use and cessation support (varenicline with counseling)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Abstinent for thirteen weeks; second course of varenicline</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Frostbite and hypothermia prevention and field treatment training</td><td>Before departure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Wilderness first aid course completed, with frostbite, hypothermia and rewarming practice</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Expedition nutrition plan: energy, weight, and vitamin C</td><td>Planned before departure, then weekly in the field</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Rations and vitamin C supply being packed; to be confirmed at the pre-departure visit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Home blood pressure average below 130/80 mmHg before departure. In progress; target 2026-05-26 [S]</item><item>No tobacco from the quit date, confirmed at each visit. In progress; target 2026-05-26 [S]</item><item>Complete a wilderness first aid course with frostbite, hypothermia and evacuation practice before departure. Outcome by 2026-04-21: Course completed, with rewarming and casualty-packaging practice [S]</item><item>A written expedition medical plan covering nutrition and vitamin C, cold injury, altitude, mental health support, medicines and evacuation, agreed before departure. In progress; target 2026-05-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Circulation 2025;152(11):e114-e218) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension monograph (2026); Wilderness Medical Society Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Prevention and Treatment of Frostbite: 2024 Update (McIntosh SE, et al. Wilderness Environ Med 2024;35(2):183-197) (2024); Wilderness Medical Society Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Out-of-Hospital Evaluation and Treatment of Accidental Hypothermia: 2019 Update (Dow J, et al. Wilderness Environ Med 2019;30(4S):S47-S69) (2019); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Pre-departure review in five weeks with electrolytes and creatinine; telephone the clinic for lightheadedness. Next scheduled visit 2026-05-26: pre-departure review: electrolytes on losartan, blood pressure, mental health, and the expedition medical plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
